.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt ED 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm ed
.Nd line-oriented text editor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s
.Op Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility edits a line buffer with the POSIX command subset.
Addresses are one-based lines, with
.Ql \&.
(current),
.Ql $
(last),
.Ql 'x
(mark),
.Ql /re/
(forward search),
.Ql ?re?
(backward search) and comma ranges.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic a , Ic i , Ic c
Append, insert or change lines until a lone
.Ql \&. .
.It Ic d , Ic p , Ic n , Ic l
Delete, print, number or escaped-print lines.
.It Ic s
Substitute with the POSIX basic regular expression syntax; flags
.Ql g ,
a numeric occurrence and
.Ql p
are supported.
.It Ic g , Ic v
Global and inverse-global matching commands.
.It Ic m , Ic t , Ic j
Move, copy or join ranges.
.It Ic k
Set a mark.
.It Ic r , Ic w , Ic e , Ic f
Read, write, edit or name a file.
.It Ic u , Ic q , Ic =
Undo, quit or print a line number.
.El
.Pp
Shell escapes
.Pq Ic !
are explicitly unsupported and return a diagnostic. The target image has no
standard-input stream, so the current wrapper expects commands on the serial
console; host tests execute the same command model directly.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
An invalid command/address exits with status 1; a usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sed 1 ,
.Xr ex 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the documented POSIX ed subset.
